Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the controller's buttons can be laid out again (TODO 240)

ps2_host_input::setPadBindings / padBindings / defaultPadBindings (PS2X_PADMAP at start): for each of the game's
pad buttons, the controller buttons that press it ("l1=l2;l2=l1;r1=r2;r2=r1"; a controller button named by its
PlayStation place). The pad read (both the native Sony path and the GLFW gamepads) collects the controller's 16
buttons, then sets the game's through the layout; the game's analog L2 / R2 (gamepadTriggers) come from the
controller trigger behind them (0 or 1 from a button). The adaptive triggers follow: triggerRequest gives each
controller trigger the effect and break point of the game trigger it presses (setTriggerRouting; an effect for a
game trigger now on a bumper is dropped), so 0152's gating stays with the click. The port's own menus read the
controller as it is.

